{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-recovery", "file": "references/iterative-recovery-lessons.md", "content": "# Iterative recovery: when the early candidate fails

A wrong ARC submission rejects the whole proposed transformation, not just a few cells. Avoid making a visually similar variation without new evidence. Reconstruct what the examples actually establish, preserve conspicuously unchanged objects as negative evidence, and request a demo only when its possible outcomes discriminate live hypotheses. After receiving a pair, synthesize it before choosing another action. Keep exact-one-action protocol formatting independent of any internal analysis.
